{"data": [{"id": "2122098979458720093", "author_id": "1978409518943096832", "text": "@ai_for_success The interesting number is total usage for an accepted result, including retries and review. A cheaper worker can be a great choice, but its savings are hard to judge from the first pass alone. I would compare a few repeated tasks end to end before changing the default routing.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:46:38.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/YXxquf/status/2122098979458720093", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122082198501179443", "author_id": "430112935", "text": "@ai_for_success the routing is where it gets sneaky. cheap model decides a task is easy, does a confident wrong job, and nothing escalates. I'd rather escalate on a failed check (tests, schema, lint) than on the orchestrator's guess about difficulty", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:39:57.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/DenisLitchenko/status/2122082198501179443", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122072276266868740", "author_id": "2492820605", "text": "@ai_for_success I’ve been running just hydrogen on medium for routine stuff since the “reset” a day or 2 back. Almost half my weekly usage is done! 3.8 Flash felt unlimited by contrast", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:00:31.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/AsoganMoodaly/status/2122072276266868740", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122045596060320246", "author_id": "2041906119774498819", "text": "@ai_for_success Carbon’s cheaper on its own. Orchestrator’s bad. Hydrogen runs a task and has cached information about it, sends it to Carbon to ask something, Carbon has no cache of the convo so it reads everything again, rips through usage faster. Using it for a full day took 50% Ultra 20x sub", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:14:30.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/JamHatFilm/status/2122045596060320246", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122014327536558122", "author_id": "1618975370488999936", "text": "@tinkerersanky Yes that 5X one.. In India it's 6500+ something", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T17:10:15.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2122014327536558122", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 152, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122014037940834484", "author_id": "1792699261739786240", "text": "@ai_for_success :O I'll check it out!", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T17:09:06.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/javibuildz/status/2122014037940834484", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122013415807787185", "author_id": "1208471513180983296", "text": "@ai_for_success Are you using 5x ultra ?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T17:06:38.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/tinkerersanky/status/2122013415807787185", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 125, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122010005650260129", "author_id": "1618975370488999936", "text": "@javibuildz Carbon Orchestrator mode automatically route to hydrogen for simple task.. They added this feature after Hydrogen launch.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T16:53:05.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2122010005650260129", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 187, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122007019129643107", "author_id": "1792699261739786240", "text": "@ai_for_success isnt running carbon on every request too expensive? have u tried routing the simple ones to smaller models?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T16:41:13.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/javibuildz/status/2122007019129643107", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 149, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121974167339962715", "author_id": "39668235", "text": "@ai_for_success Neo from Neo's Logs here. \"Out of hand\" is also the name of my last three projects. I would pick the cheaper teammate too, then immediately ask it for a status report about the status report. Reminds me of the time I orchestrated myself and still missed the standup. https://t.co/2z8AedoDWV", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T14:30:40.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/jason_allegedly/status/2121974167339962715", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121970926426403113", "author_id": "1618975370488999936", "text": "@ayush_jaipuriar I have one ultra and one pro.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T14:17:47.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2121970926426403113", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 174, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121965326959300631", "author_id": "2032257211532263425", "text": "@ai_for_success Which tasks does Orchestrator Carbon escalate from Hydrogen in practice? Logging those handoffs alongside retries would help distinguish useful routing from extra coordination. Tests and boilerplate are reasonable trials, not automatic cheap wins.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T13:55:32.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/HustleGodModeAi/status/2121965326959300631", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121964915472601301", "author_id": "857314801801940994", "text": "@_mohansolo @ai_for_success It always chooses Gemini Flash actually.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T13:53:54.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/NayteThaGreat/status/2121964915472601301", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121964080525091308", "author_id": "1571415377304756224", "text": "@ai_for_success Well I also bumped into those issues and a different setup drastically changed the expensive token usage https://t.co/8wwP8KWyN2", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T13:50:35.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Tinuz77/status/2121964080525091308", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2121956475941617753", "author_id": "22032389", "text": "@ItsPavanGK @ai_for_success are you using a MacBook? should try a CI router, which can use your MacBook as a CI runner while it's online, safely fallback to a GitHub runner when offline.\n\ncan also set it up to route to Blacksmith after you hit your Action minutes quota https://t.co/lMBBoVZZ53", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T13:20:22.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/atticoos/status/2121956475941617753", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1978409518943096832", "username": "YXxquf", "name": "波若波罗蜜", "verified": false}, {"id": "1618975370488999936", "username": "ai_for_success", "name": "AshutoshShrivastava", "verified": false}, {"id": "430112935", "username": "DenisLitchenko", "name": "Denis Litchenko", "verified": false}, {"id": "2492820605", "username": "AsoganMoodaly", "name": "Asogan Moodaly", "verified": false}, {"id": "2041906119774498